      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "What customers want from solar installation is a system which is suited to their needs.  That means first and foremost that the sales person needs to understand those needs whilst educating the customer as part of that process, and then pitch something that addresses them.  Unfortunately, too many suppliers seem have very fixed ideas about what they sell and show limited interest in working with the customer to consider those needs - or to appropriately reset their expectations when necessary.Happily, Frank at Advanced All Energy has a team which does put the customer at the centre of their process.  From Dan who dealt with sales, through to the installation team who were outstanding, the engagement and quality of service was excellent.The system itself provides a balance between quality and price which makes sense given the rapid pace of change in the space.  I saw little point in paying a premium for 25 year panel product warranties when I fully expect something better and cheaper will probably be available long before (and who knows what the energy market will look like in even 5 years!).AAE's quote wasn't the cheapest (but not exorbitant either), and they don't provide much \"hand-holding\" after-sales, but for simpler solar installations little is required and the team are just a phone call away if needed.  So overall, I'd recommend them as people you can place some trust in if you're looking for solar PV.",
